Package: polyDx
Type: Package
Title: Diagnostics for Dominance-Labelled Variance in Polyploid Genomic Prediction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jinguang", "Tong", email = "ton068@csiro.au", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tools for deciding whether the variance a polyploid genomic model
    assigns to a dominance kernel reflects biological digenic dominance or is an
    artefact of near-collinear additive and dominance kernels. Provides orthogonal
    degree-wise relationship kernels (additive, digenic, trigenic, quadrigenic and
    higher) built from allele dosage, kernel-geometry diagnostics, and the
    panel-conditioned diagnostic workflow: negative (additive-only), positive
    (digenic spike-in), structure and permutation controls all generated and
    fitted on the empirical panel's own genotype matrix, plus the rule-based
    scorecard that turns those controls into a per-panel verdict.
